d 'FREEIV': module for instrument-free estimation of a linear structural model with an endogenous regressor
d
d  freeiv estimates the coefficient on an endogenous regressor
d without an external instrument, in the linear triangular model in
d which a single latent confounder generates the endogeneity. Under
d scale consistency -- the confounder moves the outcome directly by
d exactly as much as it moves it through the regressor -- the
d second moments of the data leave one number free, and the
d coefficient lies between half the least-squares slope and that
d slope: an interval that assumes nothing more and is exactly the
d set of values for which the implied variances are non-negative.
d The routes of the command impose the same linear structure on the
d moments of the next orders: at order three the quadratic moment
d estimator (the default) and a closed form for symmetric noise; at
d order four a joint and a profiled GMM, each with a Hansen J, and
d the region where the profiled J stays within 3.84 of its minimum.
d A second indicator of the same confounder frees the confounder's
d direct loading and turns scale consistency into a test. The
d estimators of Lewbel, Schennach and Zhang (2024) and of Lewbel
d (2012), the Gaussian copula, the rank control function and the
d coefficient-stability adjustment of Oster (2019) are computed on
d the same data and judged by the same interval. Standard errors
d come from the influence functions of the moments, with pweights
d in sandwich form and Taylor linearization over a survey design
d declared by svyset (vce(svy)). Companion commands report what the
d data can carry before any estimation (freeivmenu), what a value
d of the coefficient implies about the unobservables (freeivdiag),
d tests of endogeneity and of the agreement between routes
d (freeivtest), and all of it in one table (freeivreport); a dialog
d box is included, and the examples of the help run from clickable
d links (freeiv_examples). The paper that documents the models and
d the command is included as an ancillary file (freeiv_paper.pdf). 
d
d KW:  endogeneity
d KW: instrument-free estimation
d KW: latent confounder
d KW: higher-order moments
d KW: partial identification
d KW: GMM
d KW: survey design
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261009
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar,  Universite Laval 
d Support: email aabd@@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
